-- title:
--   Finitely many Kᵥ^× G₀-cosets of twist-bounded units
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra such that $L/K$ is Galois, and let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $\tau \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ lies in the subgroup of integral powers of $\sigma$ (so the Galois group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$, write $K_v$ for the associated adic completion and put $E = L \otimes_K K_v$, and let $\mathrm{sigmaTensor}$ denote the ring endomorphism of $E$ induced by $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}_{K_v}$. Let $G_0 \subseteq E$ be compact and open, containing $1$, closed under multiplication, and such that every $g \in G_0$ has an inverse $h \in G_0$ with $gh = 1$. The assertion is that there is a finite set $F$ of elements of $E$, each of them a unit, such that: for every unit $c$ of $E$ for which $(\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(c) = cg$ for some $g \in G_0$, there exist $f \in F$, a nonzero $x \in K_v$ and $g \in G_0$ with $c = f \cdot \mathrm{alg}(x) \cdot g$, where $\mathrm{alg}$ is the structure map $K_v \to E$.
--
--   This is the finiteness statement that the units of $L \otimes_K K_v$ whose $\sigma$-twisted quotient lies in the compact open unit group $G_0$ form finitely many cosets of $K_v^\times G_0$; it rests on the description of the kernel and of the norm-one image of $c \mapsto (\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id})(c)/c$ (Hilbert 90 over the local ring $E$) together with compactness. It feeds the volume estimates for fibres of the twisted orbital computations, being cited by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_withDensity_norm_inv_setOf_norm_mem_and_mul_sigmaTensor_eq_mul_mul_le`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_forall_withDensity_norm_inv_setOf_norm_mem_and_mul_sigmaTensor_eq_mul_mul_le) and by [`AutomorphicForm.exists_isCompact_forall_exists_includeRight_mul_mem_of_sigmaTensor_mul_inv_mem_adicCompletion`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.exists_isCompact_forall_exists_includeRight_mul_mem_of_sigmaTensor_mul_inv_mem_adicCompletion).
